{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"reasoning","text":"**Formulating minimal LRU eviction with metric callback**\n\nI'll implement evict_idle using min to find and remove the least recently used connection, compute idle_seconds, then conditionally call a callable emit_metric attribute on self if set, to emit the \"pool.connection.evicted\" metric with idle_seconds as a tag—this keeps the fix minimal while satisfying metric emission expectations within given constraints."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"code\": \"    def evict_idle(self) -> Connection | None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Remove the least-recently-used idle connection.\\n\\n        BUG_47: uses ``self.connections.pop(0)`` which removes the\\n        *first-inserted* connection (FIFO order) rather than the one\\n        with the oldest ``last_used_at`` timestamp (LRU order).  When\\n        connections are touched out of insertion order, the wrong\\n        connection is evicted.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if not self.connections:\\n            return None\\n\\n        now = time.time()\\n\\n        # BUG_47: FIFO eviction — should find the conn with min(last_used_at)\\n        evicted = min(self.connections, key=lambda conn: conn.last_used_at)\\n        self.connections.remove(evicted)\\n\\n        idle_seconds = now - evicted.last_used_at\\n        emitter = getattr(self, \\\"emit_metric\\\", None)\\n        if callable(emitter):\\n            emitter(\\\"pool.connection.evicted\\\", idle_seconds=idle_seconds)\\n\\n        return evicted\", \"comments\": \"select the LRU connection for eviction and fire the pool.connection.evicted metric hook if one exists\"}"}}
